  "rings_about": "Per designation: r = smallest chamfer of the ring corners (r_s min of the dimension series); da_min = smallest diameter of a shoulder that holds the inner ring; Da_max = largest bore of a shoulder that holds the outer ring. da_min = d + 2 h and Da_max = D - 2 h with h from shoulder_height_min. A shoulder that ends inside the chamfer holds nothing. The corner of a printed seat is sharper than r, or relieved, so the ring lands on the shoulder and not on the corner. The ring's own shoulder diameters (where the seal or the cage begins) are not here: they differ from maker to maker.",
