  "shields_tag": "D",
  "shields_about": "Per designation, where the shield or seal of a capped bearing begins: d1 = the shoulder diameter of the inner ring (the shield stands just outside it), D2 = the recess diameter of the outer ring (the shield sits inside it). A clamp washer on the inner ring reaches at most to d1, one on the outer ring at most to D2: further on it presses the shield onto the inner ring (washers.landing). Where a designation has no row here, a washer that reaches past the ISO land of its ring (da_min, Da_max of \"rings\") is not judged (NOT_RUN) until its row is added. A project replaces a row by the sheet of the bearing in hand: gate/owner/tables.json \"bearings\": {\"shields\": {\"608\": {\"d1\": ..., \"D2\": ..., \"source\": ..., \"date\": ...}}}.",
  "shields_source": "Approximate values (the \"about\" figures of the capped variants -2Z / -2RZ in deep groove ball bearing catalogues), written down from reference knowledge for the sizes a first project used, rounded towards the shield; not measured and not checked against one maker's sheet. They differ from maker to maker by a few tenths: confirm a row against the sheet of the bearing you bought before a clamp depends on it.",
