  "aliases_about": "Other names of a row. 618xx and 619xx are the five-digit names of 68xx and 69xx. Miniature bearings (bore under 10) are wider with shields or seals than open: the capped width has its own row with the suffix ZZ, and -2Z and -2RS name the same size.",
  "source": "Boundary dimensions and chamfers of the metric dimension series 18, 19, 10 and 02 (ISO 15) and the shoulder heights makers publish for them, written down from reference knowledge of the standard; no row was measured on a bearing. Check a row against the sheet of the bearing you bought before a seat depends on its chamfer or shoulder."
